{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Current behaviour\n\nThe runs list is only re-fetched automatically while `has_active()` is true (a queued / in_progress run exists) — see `on_tick` in `src/github/state.rs`. Once every run is completed, a newly started run does not show up until `r` is pressed. The issue / PR lists detect changes through a conditional (ETag) request to `/issues?sort=updated&per_page=1`, but that probe cannot see a run starting.\n\n## Proposal\n\nAdd a change check for runs, built the same way as the issue / PR one.\n\n- Every `github-poll-interval`, request `repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/runs?per_page=1` with `If-None-Match`\n- 304: do nothing (not counted against the rate limit)\n- 200: store the new ETag and re-fetch the runs list\n- Idle ×6 / low-quota ×2 / stop, the rate-limit backoff and `github-auto-refresh \"off\"` apply as they do today\n- The 5s re-fetch while a run is active stays as is (the probe may be skipped during that time)\n- Add the probe to the fixture recording (`vig fixtures record`), keeping only status / ETag / body\n\n## Cost\n\nOne list fetch = 2 REST requests (`/actions/runs` + `/actions/workflows`, measured with `GH_DEBUG=api`). The probe costs 0 when nothing changed and +2 only on a change. Everything is on the REST core quota (5000/h); no GraphQL points are spent.\n\n## What changes\n\nWith the GitHub page left open, a newly started run appears in the list without pressing `r`. Nothing else changes.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-10-15T05:45:18Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":196,"state":"CLOSED","title":"GitHub page: auto-refresh the workflow runs list even when no run is active"}
